WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:08.060
So, let's move on to the components of the system's architecture, namely the portal

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.680
for working with translations.

3
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:16.830
What is it? It's this address here, the main one we work with,

4
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:22.750
and we'll just take a quick look at the four

5
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.970
pages we have.

6
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.690
More detail on working with them will come in separate videos on each topic.

7
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.960
What's here? On the home page we can search and also filter by category.

8
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:47.080
In the left corner there is a special feature: if we have

9
00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.520
an alternative version,

10
00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:57.260
which is called a branch, of this portal, or

11
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.400
of the list of talks,

12
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.040
or even of a translation,

13
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.840
you can select it here.

14
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.660
It's an advanced, more technical thing that you won't need at first, just so you

15
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:12.880
know that it's here.

16
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:21.600
At the top right we can refresh the page. If some

17
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.060
new feature has come to this page but you still have an older version saved locally,

18
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.240
then here is the "Check for updates" button.

19
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.620
You can switch languages and you can switch styles.

20
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.260
You can choose a "Dark" or "Light" theme.

21
00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:44.950
That's about this page. On this page you can search by

22
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.090
date, by title,

23
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:56.320
when you want to find, for example, among all the talks that are in

24
00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:01.380
the system. That is, whether the one you need is there at all, whether it has already been added to

25
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:06.540
the system. You can also switch to "Expert mode": at the bottom right we click the

26
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:12.820
dot, and then a few more categories appear, including the ones that are still

27
00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:19.740
pending, not fully ready for proofreading yet, but already in the system.

28
00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.940
For example, we want to find some Ganesha Puja.

29
00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.580
See, we have only 5:

30
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.530
one is already "approved",

31
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:40.470
one is "in review", and three are still "pending" – not for review, but waiting to become technically

32
00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.830
ready.

33
00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:50.830
In expert mode it shows what is missing for it to become ready for

34
00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.430
review. For example, the subtitles are missing.

35
00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.160
That's about the home page.

36
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.280
Next we have the "+ Add Talk" button, which is exactly the feature for adding new talks.

37
00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.440
We'll record a separate short video about it; in short, this is the button.

38
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:19.520
Next we have dates: if we click on a date,

39
00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.400
we get to Amruta.

40
00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.540
And here, accordingly, we can look at some other...

41
00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.080
never mind, we can look in other languages.

42
00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.900
Something else in another video source, that is, it's just a link to Amruta.

43
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:44.500
We have the "View translation" button, the so-called preview button, and "Review translation", the review one.

44
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.860
They have similar functionality, just implemented differently, each with its own

45
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:56.840
features. Let's take a look, so that each of you can understand which

46
00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:03.040
button suits you better, or at least try both of them in order

47
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.040
to choose.

48
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:12.480
"View translation" puts the priority on watching the video in real time

49
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:19.110
or listening. In this case, if there is no video, listening

50
00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.710
and either making notes as you go,

51
00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.870
or making edits as you go.

52
00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:33.380
What does it look like? For example, let's take "Markers": here we are listening, at some point we

53
00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:39.270
realised that something needs doing here. We pressed

54
00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:43.230
"Mark",

55
00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:50.820
on this subtitle here we added, wrote something:

56
00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:56.070
"Needs work".

57
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.400
This is the marker feature: when we press "Mark", the video pauses,

58
00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:09.520
and the cursor is here – we can quickly type something or type nothing at all, the mark

59
00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.980
stays. Then we press Enter, and the video keeps playing.

60
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.080
What is the approach here?

61
00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:28.160
That first we can simply tune in to this talk. We sat down

62
00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:34.900
and listened to it, just now, you could say. And, for example, during

63
00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:41.780
viewing we noticed that something needs fixing here, and we

64
00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.080
simply dropped markers.

65
00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:50.320
And, for example, after watching this hour and a half we have 20 marks, which later

66
00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:57.180
we can come back to separately and work on each, perhaps another time. That's one way

67
00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.180
of working.

68
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:02.980
Also

69
00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.780
what else can we do here?

70
00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.340
You can also choose additional English subtitles.

71
00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:15.780
Then we'll see what is shown in the original subtitles, and also in our

72
00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:21.900
translated ones. So you can find some mismatch, or you can also find,

73
00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.220
by the way,

74
00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.000
a mismatch between the English subtitles and what is being said.

75
00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:35.040
So if we find something like that, please also note it separately, we will

76
00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.440
fix the English too, and send the corrections in English.

77
00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.020
The only thing the system doesn't provide right now is editing the English

78
00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.120
right away.

79
00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:52.560
But please at least note it, let us know, and along the way we'll also improve

80
00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.090
the English subtitles if they don't match the speech. That's the marking mode.

81
00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:05.670
And the editing mode is similar. While watching, we can simply press

82
00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:10.530
"Edit". The subtitle appears right away. Here's the original, here you can

83
00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:17.190
edit it. For example, we removed a comma – here's our edit, and we pressed Enter,

84
00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:22.570
and our player automatically went on playing.

85
00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.950
You also need to understand

86
00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:34.170
that once we edited, our subtitles were edited right here as well.

87
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:41.660
Back. And this feature can accordingly be used to show

88
00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:46.520
right away. For example, an automatic translation has appeared – we looked through it here, edited it

89
00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:52.220
right away, we ended up with 20 edits. We're not sending them to the system yet, it's not yet on

90
00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:57.720
Amruta, not on YouTube, nowhere. But your version already exists, it's still only on your computer

91
00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:02.780
for now. But it can already be played in full screen. We press the

92
00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:09.480
full-screen button, and we see this

93
00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:15.100
version. The only thing is, right now I'm not recording the whole

94
00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:19.000
screen, so the subtitles are a little hard to see.

95
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.140
This is how it will look.

96
00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.220
The subtitles are shown right away in full screen,

97
00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:32.360
the player controls below are not caught in the recording here.

98
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:39.440
This is something you can use right away for a demonstration, without sending

99
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.900
anywhere even your own edited copy.

100
00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.060
This

101
00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.180
page, that's how it's useful, and those are its nuances and advantages.

102
00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.360
The translation review page.

103
00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.630
It has a few things here... Let's take a different one.

104
00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.790
A slightly different focus.

105
00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.700
By default it looks like this, that is, we have the transcript divided into paragraphs:

106
00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:15.120
on the left the original, on the right the automatic translation.

107
00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:22.820
So we can go ahead and edit it as text, simply reading

108
00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.560
the original and looking at the translation.

109
00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:30.770
But on this page we have extra options – we can choose "subtitles"

110
00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:38.760
and work with subtitles in a format where the page shows at once what came before

111
00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:44.060
and what comes after. So this format is a little different.

112
00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:51.060
Here we focus more on the text of the original and the translation.

113
00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.220
But there is also the "Show video" button.

114
00:09:54.220 --> 00:10:00.560
It is remembered for each talk, and you can

115
00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:04.990
resize it. And what happens here?

116
00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.070
In the same way, we

117
00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.730
start it,

118
00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.420
and we get the link-up, this highlight, jumping along automatically.

119
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:28.220
If we need to edit, we click, the video stops automatically, we

120
00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.000
make the corrections, removed a comma,

121
00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.210
and we can press Enter.

122
00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:41.350
Then the video plays on. That's how it works in "subtitles" mode. And in the same way, in

123
00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.510
"transcript" mode you can open the video.

124
00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:52.560
And it will be the same: there will be blocks of text, like this, and

125
00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:59.330
they will be highlighted. You can edit in the same way. So, these are the two pages, their

126
00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:01.630
differences and features.

127
00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:04.550
Choose for yourselves what is convenient for you,

128
00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:11.490
and send feedback on what is worth adding, removing, changing,

129
00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.190
improving.

130
00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:19.850
There will be separate videos on how to send changes to the system, and so on.
